<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Proclamation of the Russian Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1721">1721</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The proclamation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a> took place in 1721, when the Senate conferred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter I</a> the titles of Emperor of All <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, Peter the Great and Father of the Fatherland. It followed Russia's victory over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a> and the acquisition of Baltic territories. The act formally marked the beginning of the Russian Empire.</p></div>
